================================================================================
Third-Party Open Source Software Notices and Acknowledgments
================================================================================

This project distinguishes between runtime dependencies (code directly used)
and projects from which conceptual workflows or design patterns were referenced:

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Part A: Direct Runtime Dependencies (Libraries Used in Scripts)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The following open-source software packages are included as dependencies and
invoked during Markdown parsing and PDF generation:

1. KaTeX
   Repository: https://github.com/KaTeX/KaTeX
   License: MIT License
   Copyright (c) 2013-2025 Khan Academy and other contributors
   Usage: LaTeX mathematical typesetting engine and web fonts.

2. Marked
   Repository: https://github.com/markedjs/marked
   License: MIT License
   Copyright (c) 2011-2025 Christopher Jeffrey and other contributors
   Usage: High-performance Markdown syntax compiler.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Part B: Workflow & Conceptual Acknowledgments (No Direct Code Duplicated)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The following open-source projects provided conceptual inspiration, workflow
architecture, and prompt structuring ideas for academic writing skills. Their
ideas are gratefully acknowledged under the MIT License, though their source code
has not been directly bundled:

1. aniketkrs/research-paper
   Repository: https://github.com/aniketkrs/research-paper
   License: MIT License
   Copyright (c) 2024-2025 Aniket Kumar
   Acknowledgment: Inspired the "Plan-Before-Write" structured workflow.

2. lishix520/academic-paper-skills
   Repository: https://github.com/lishix520/academic-paper-skills
   License: MIT License
   Copyright (c) 2024-2025 lishix520
   Acknowledgment: Referenced multi-stage agent writing workflow patterns.

3. WenyuChiou/academic-writing-skills
   Repository: https://github.com/WenyuChiou/academic-writing-skills
   License: MIT License
   Copyright (c) 2024-2025 Wenyu Chiou
   Acknowledgment: Referenced academic style guides and review methodologies.

